# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# --- environments ---
.venv/
venv/

# --- build output ---
# NOT `build/` wholesale: build/build.py, build/native.py and
# build/installer.iss are source and must be committed. Only the
# generated output is ignored.
build/dist/
build/work/
build/installer/
build/release/
dist/
*.spec

# build/native.py unpacks and compiles the Tier 2 libraries here. It is
# fetched-and-verified third-party source plus CMake output -- 132 MB of
# it, and every generated Makefile records the ABSOLUTE build path, so
# committing it would publish the build machine's directory layout. The
# DLLs it produces are installed to app/assets/native/ and those ARE
# committed; this tree is reproducible from native.py whenever needed.
build/thirdparty/

# --- generated benchmark input ---
# benchmarks/corpus.py builds these from pinned or seeded inputs. They
# are INPUT to the harness, not results: sourcetree is a copy of this
# very source tree and sitepackages a copy of the venv, so committing
# them would duplicate the repository inside itself. RESULTS.md and
# results.json are the outputs worth keeping and are NOT ignored.
benchmarks/corpora/

# --- compiled engine ---
# The .pyd and the C it is generated from are proprietary output. The
# C in particular is a near-complete transcription of the engine source
# and must never reach the public repository.
*.pyd
*.so
*.c

# --- spike artefacts (throwaway by definition) ---
spikes/build/
spikes/dist/
spikes/*.spec

# --- proprietary: must never enter the public repository ---
# The routing engine and the trained dictionary corpus live in the
# private compakt-engine repository. These entries are a backstop in
# case anyone copies one in by accident.
core/compressor.py
dictionaries/
*.pakt-dict

# --- local ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log
